"""TLV7041DBVR - nanopower comparator, open-drain output, SOT-23-5. Bare part.

Datasheet: TI SLVSE13J (September 2017, revised November 2024), TLV703x/TLV704x.

Pins (section 4, Table 4-1, SOT-23): 1 OUT, 2 V-, 3 IN+, 4 IN-, 5 V+.

Absolute maximum ratings (section 5.1, p6): supply -0.3 to 7 V; IN+ and IN- V- - 0.3 to 7 V
whatever the supply (diode-clamped to V- only), input current +-10 mA; OUT (TLV704x) V- - 0.3
to 7 V.
Recommended operating conditions (section 5.3): supply 1.6 to 6.5 V; input voltage V- - 0.1 to
V+ + 0.1 V.

Electrical characteristics (section 5.7, single, VS 1.8-5 V, -40 to 125 C): input offset
+-0.1 / +-8 mV; hysteresis 2 / 7 / 17 mV (25 C); input bias 2 pA; open-drain leakage 100 pA;
supply current 335 / 900 nA.

Function (section 6.4): OUT is high impedance while IN+ > IN-, low while IN+ < IN-. Power-on
reset: while the supply is below its minimum, rising or falling, the TLV704x holds OUT high
impedance (logical high).

Integrator-owned circuitry (section 7.3): 100 nF bypass capacitor from V+ to V- when the supply
is noisy or far away; the output pull-up.
"""

# Section 5.3: recommended supply 1.6-6.5 V.
VCC = io(Power(voltage="1.6V to 6.5V"))
GND = io(Ground)
IN_P = io(Net)
IN_N = io(Net)
OUT = io(Net)

Component(
    name="TLV7041",
    prefix="U",
    symbol=Symbol(library="TLV7041DBVR.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("SOT-23-5.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="TLV7041DBVR", manufacturer="Texas Instruments"),
    pins={
        "OUT": OUT,
        "V-": GND,
        "+": IN_P,
        "-": IN_N,
        "V+": VCC,
    },
)
